{
  "_about": "The golden vector for the archive's readable copy. contract/DATA-CONTRACT.md 8.5 and issues #9 and B4. B4 dropped the emulator on the argument that data survival is proven by the round trip against golden vectors in continuous integration rather than by a long lived phone installation, and until this file existed nothing in continuous integration rendered a readable page at all: the regeneration test needs a device and the date vectors are an instrumented test. This is the half that can run without one. Rows in, bytes out, on every push. The rows were taken from a real archive the app wrote, so they are rows the app itself could write, and between them they exercise every one of the twelve rendering decisions. The expected pages are in expected/<locale>/ and they are regenerated deliberately, never automatically: a diff here means the archive's permanent text or its layout changed, which is a decision rather than an accident.",
  "counts": [
    1,
